title: "Recover from crashes and restarts"
output: rmarkdown::html_vignette
vignette: >
  %\VignetteIndexEntry{Recover from crashes and restarts}
  %\VignetteEngine{knitr::rmarkdown}
  %\VignetteEncoding{UTF-8}
---

```{r setup, include = FALSE}
source("tools/guides/setup.R")
```

Coordination state lives in one DuckDB file that only the endpoint writes.
Pi sessions, harness hosts, and the endpoint process itself may all die
between two calls. This guide kills things on purpose and shows what
survives.

```{bash}
start_endpoint() {
  node tools/pi-coordination-endpoint.ts \
    "$STATE/coordination.url" "$STATE/coordination.duckdb" >> "$STATE/endpoint.log" 2>&1 &
  echo $! > "$STATE/endpoint.pid"
  until [ -s "$STATE/coordination.url" ]; do sleep 0.1; done
}
declare -f start_endpoint > "$STATE/functions.sh"
start_endpoint
```

## A crash in the middle of a delivery

`bob` receives a message under a two-second lease and does not acknowledge
it. Then the endpoint is killed without a chance to shut down:

```{r}
url <- guide_url()
alice <- register("alice")
bob <- rpc_call(url, "register", list(
  project_id = "guide", agent_id = "bob", instance_id = "session-1",
  operation_key = "start", adapter_kind = "pi_extension",
  delivery_capability = "api_acceptance"
))
sent <- rpc_call(url, "send", list(
  registration_id = alice$registration_id, recipient_agent_id = "bob",
  idempotency_key = "report", content = "Summarize yesterday's run."
))
leased <- rpc_call(url, "receive", list(
  registration_id = bob$registration_id, visibility_timeout_ms = 2000
))$messages[[1]]
identical(leased$message_id, sent$message_id)
```

```{bash}
kill -9 "$(cat "$STATE/endpoint.pid")"
sleep 1
. "$STATE/functions.sh"
rm "$STATE/coordination.url"
start_endpoint
echo "restarted"
```

The restarted endpoint listens on the same `ipc://` address, so clients need no
new configuration. Registrations and mail were in the database file.
Once the lease runs out, the same message comes back with a new receipt:

```{r}
identical(guide_url(), url)
Sys.sleep(2.1)
redelivered <- rpc_call(url, "receive", list(registration_id = bob$registration_id))$messages[[1]]
c(same_message = identical(redelivered$message_id, sent$message_id),
  new_receipt = !identical(redelivered$receipt_token, leased$receipt_token))
```

This is at-least-once delivery. An agent that did the work before the crash
sees the message again, so the work itself must tolerate running twice.

## What an acknowledgement proves

A registration declares how strong its acknowledgements are, and each
acknowledgement records that declaration. The Pi extension declares
`api_acceptance`: Pi's public API accepted the message into the conversation.
A host-owned `AgentHarness` lane declares `harness_lane_commit`, because the
message was committed to a durable lane before the acknowledgement:

```{r}
acked <- rpc_call(url, "ack", list(
  registration_id = bob$registration_id, receipt_token = redelivered$receipt_token,
  delivery_ref = "steer:session-1"
))
show(acked, c("acknowledged", "delivery_capability", "receiver_instance_id"))
lane <- rpc_call(url, "register", list(
  project_id = "guide", agent_id = "bob", instance_id = "host-lane",
  operation_key = "lane", adapter_kind = "agent_harness",
  delivery_capability = "harness_lane_commit"
))
lane$delivery_capability
```

Neither is exactly-once execution. Each says only which boundary the message
had crossed when it was acknowledged.

## Mail nobody reads

Mail sent to a mailbox that nobody drains becomes a dead letter at the end of
its time to live. Here the time to live is the one-minute minimum:

```{r}
lost <- rpc_call(url, "send", list(
  registration_id = alice$registration_id, recipient_agent_id = "nobody",
  idempotency_key = "lost", content = "Anyone there?", ttl_ms = 60000
))
lost$recipient_seen
Sys.sleep(61)
nobody <- register("nobody")
length(rpc_call(url, "receive", list(registration_id = nobody$registration_id))$messages)
```

Dead letters, like acknowledged mail, are deleted 30 days after they end.
With the endpoint stopped, the database file shows every state:

```{bash}
kill "$(cat "$STATE/endpoint.pid")"
sleep 1
```

```{r}
connection <- DBI::dbConnect(suppressMessages(duckdb::duckdb()),
  dbdir = file.path(guide_state, "coordination.duckdb"), read_only = TRUE)
DBI::dbGetQuery(connection,
  "SELECT recipient_agent_id, state FROM coordination_messages ORDER BY created_at_ms")
DBI::dbDisconnect(connection, shutdown = TRUE)
```

```{r, include = FALSE}
stopifnot(
  identical(redelivered$message_id, sent$message_id),
  identical(acked$delivery_capability, "api_acceptance")
)
```

```{r, echo = FALSE, results = "asis"}
cat("> GUIDE_DURABILITY_VERIFIED: a killed endpoint redelivers the leased message and keeps dead letters\n")
```
